                <img srcset=\"content/images/size/w160/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-14-at-12.28.19-1.png 160w,\n                           content/images/size/w320/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-14-at-12.28.19-1.png 320w,\n                          content/images/size/w600/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-14-at-12.28.19-1.png 600w,\n                         content/images/size/w960/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-14-at-12.28.19-1.png 960w,\n                        content/images/size/w1200/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-14-at-12.28.19-1.png 1200w,\n                       content/images/size/w2000/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-14-at-12.28.19-1.png1.png 2000w\" sizes=\"320px\" src=\"content/images/size/w600/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-14-at-12.28.19-1.png\" alt=\"Automatic Threat Modeling with pytm and Github Actions\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            </figure>\n        <div class=\"gh-card-wrapper\">\n            <h3 class=\"gh-card-title is-title\">Automatic Threat Modeling with pytm and Github Actions</h3>\n                    <p class=\"gh-card-excerpt is-body\">pytm is a OWASP tool that integrates with a custom GPT to make the threat modeling process quicker and more automated.\n\nI've developed a custom Github Action that, on every Pull Request event, generates or updates a Threat Model report, based on changes to the Python files generated</p>\n            <footer class=\"gh-card-meta\">\n<!--\n             -->\n                    <span class=\"gh-card-author\">By Inês Martins</span>\n                    <time class=\"gh-card-date\" datetime=\"2024-11-14\">14 Nov 2024</time>\n                <!--\n         --></footer>\n        </div>\n    </a>","link":"https://inesmartins.github.io/automate-threat-modeling-with-pytm-and-github-actions/index.html","retrieved":1731542400000},{"title":"HTB Write-up | FormulaX (user-only)","contents":"<a class=\"gh-card-link\" href=\"htb-writeup-formulax/index.html\">\n            <fig