ot-2024-11-13-at-13.35.59.png 1200w,\n                       content/images/size/w2000/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.35.59.png9.png 2000w\" sizes=\"320px\" src=\"content/images/size/w600/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.35.59.png\" alt=\"HTB Write-up | iClean (user-only)\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            </figure>\n        <div class=\"gh-card-wrapper\">\n            <h3 class=\"gh-card-title is-title\">HTB Write-up | iClean (user-only)</h3>\n                <p class=\"gh-card-excerpt is-body\">Write-up for iClean, a retired HTB Linux machine.</p>\n            <footer class=\"gh-card-meta\">\n<!--\n             -->\n                    <span class=\"gh-card-author\">By Inês Martins</span>\n                    <time class=\"gh-card-date\" datetime=\"2024-08-04\">04 Aug 2024</time>\n                <!--\n         --></footer>\n        </div>\n    </a>","link":"https://inesmartins.github.io/htb-writeup-iclean/index.html","retrieved":1722729600000},{"title":"Exploiting SSRF in Kubernetes","contents":"<a class=\"gh-card-link\" href=\"exploiting-ssrf-in-k8s-environment/index.html\">\n            <figure class=\"gh-card-image\">\n                <img srcset=\"content/images/size/w160/format/webp/2024/04/6.png 160w,\n                           content/images/size/w320/format/webp/2024/04/6.png 320w,\n                          content/images/size/w600/format/webp/2024/04/6.png 600w,\n                         content/images/size/w960/format/webp/2024/04/6.png 960w,\n                        content/images/size/w1200/format/webp/2024/04/6.png 1200w,\n                       content/images/size/w2000/format/webp/2024/04/6.png6.png 2000w\" sizes=\"320px\" src=\"content/images/size/w600/2024/04/6.png\" alt=\"Exploiting SSRF in Kubernetes\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            </figure>\n        <div class=\"gh-card-wrapper\">\n            <h3 class=\"gh-card-title is-title\">Exploiting SSRF in Kubernetes</h3>\n                    <p class=\"gh-card-excerpt is-body\">While testing an API that was exposed to the Internet, I found an unauthorised SSRF vulnerability that allowed me to trick the server into performing any GET request using http or https protocol.\n\nI had access to the response (i.e.: this wasn't a blind SSRF), full control</p>\n            <footer class=\"gh-card-meta\">\n<!--\n             -->\n                    <span class=\"gh-card-author\">By Inês Martins</span>\n                    <time class=\"gh-card-date\" datetime=\"2024-04-01\">01 Apr 2024</time>\n                <!--\n         --></footer>\n        </div>\n    </a>","link":"https://inesmartins.github.io/exploiting-ssrf-in-k8s-environment/index.html","retrieved":1711929600000},{"title":"HTB Write-up | Vessel (user-only)","contents":"<a class=\"gh-card-link\" href=\"htb-write-up-vessel/index.html\">\n            <figure class=\"gh-card-image\">\n                <img srcset=\"content/images/size/w160/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.36.11.png 160w,\n                           content/images/size/w320/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.36.11.png 320w,\n                          content/images/size/w600/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.36.11.png 600w,\n                         content/images/size/w960/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.36.11.png 960w,\n                        content/images/size/w1200/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.36.11.png 1200w,\n                       content/images/size/w2000/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.36.11.png1.png 2000w\" sizes=\"320px\" src=\"content/images/size/w600/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.36.11.png\" alt=\"HTB Write-up | Vessel (user-only)\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            </figure>\n        <div class=\"gh-card-wrapper\">\n            <h3 class=\"gh-card-title is-title\">HTB Write-up | Vessel (user-only)</h3>\n                <p class=\"gh-card-excerpt is-body\">Write-up for Vessel, a retired HTB Linux machine.</p>\n            <footer class=\"gh-card-meta\">\n<!--\n             -->\n                    <span class=\"gh-card-author\">By Inês Martins</span>\n                    <time class=\"gh-card-date\" datetime=\"2022-11-12\">12 Nov 2022</time>\n                <!--\n         --></footer>\n        </div>\n    </a>","link":"https://inesmartins.github.io/htb-write-up-vessel/index.html","retrieved":1668211200000},{"title":"Exfiltrating data from Android applications via WebView Takeover (Open Redirect)","contents":"<a class=\"gh-card-link\" href=\"exfiltrating-data-via-webview-takeover/index.html\">\n            <figure class=\"gh-card-image\">\n                <img srcset=\"content/images/size/w160/format/webp/2022/10/maxresdefault-1-1.jpeg 160w,\n                           content/images/size/w320/format/webp/2022/10/maxresdefault-1-1.jpeg 320w,\n                          content/images/size/w600/format/webp/2022/10/maxresdefault-1-1.jpeg 600w,\n                         content/images/size/w960/format/webp/2022/10/maxresdefault-1-1.jpeg 960w,\n                        content/images/size/w1200/format/webp/2022/10/maxresdefault-1-1.jpeg 1200w,\n                       content/images/size/w2000/format/webp/2022/10/maxresdefault-1-1.jpeg.jpeg 2000w\" sizes=\"320px\" src=\"content/images/size/w600/2022/10/maxresdefault-1-1.jpeg\" alt=\"Exfiltrating data from Android applications via WebView Takeover (Open Redirect)\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            </figure>\n        <div class=\"gh-card-wrapper\">\n            <h3 class=\"gh-card-title is-title\">Exfiltrating data from Android applications via WebView Takeover (Open Redirect)</h3>\n                <p class=\"gh-card-excerpt is-body\">In this article, I go through the scenarios in which I've been able to exfiltrate data from real Android applications, after detecting a WebView takeover (aka \"Open Redirect\") vulnerability.</p>\n            <footer class=\"gh-card-meta\">\n<!--\n             -->\n                    <span class=\"gh-card-author\">By Inês Martins</span>\n                    <time class=\"gh-card-date\" datetime=\"2022-10-06\">06 Oct 2022</time>\n                <!--\n         --></footer>\n        </div>\n    </a>","link":"https://inesmartins.github.io/exfiltrating-data-via-webview-takeover/index.html","retrieved":1665014400000},{"title":"DataStore is the new SharedPreferences, old vulns still apply","contents":"<a class=\"gh-card-link\" href=\"when-not-to-use-jetpack-datastore/index.html\">\n            <figure class=\"gh-card-image\">\n                <img srcset=\"content/images/size/w160/format/webp/2022/09/3.jpeg 160w,\n                           content/images/size/w320/format/webp/2022/09/3.jpeg 320w,\n                          content/images/size/w600/format/webp/2022/09/3.jpeg 600w,\n                         content/images/size/w960/format/webp/2022/09/3.jpeg 960w,\n                        content/images/size/w1200/format/webp/2022/09/3.jpeg 1200w,\n                       content/images/size/w2000/format/webp/2022/09/3.jpeg.jpeg 2000w\" sizes=\"320px\" src=\"content/images/size/w600/2022/09/3.jpeg\" alt=\"DataStore is the new SharedPreferences, old vulns still apply\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            </figure>\n        <div class=\"gh-card-wrapper\">\n            <h3 class=\"gh-card-title is-title\">DataStore is the new SharedPreferences, old vulns still apply</h3>\n                <p class=\"gh-card-excerpt is-body\">Neither DataStore nor SharedPreferences should be used to persist sensitive data ... but as we know, Insecure Data Storage is one of the most common vulnerabilities found in mobile applications.</p>\n            <footer class=\"gh-card-meta\">\n<!--\n             -->\n                    <span class=\"gh-card-author\">By Inês Martins</span>\n                    <time class=\"gh-card-date\" datetime=\"2022-09-15\">15 Sep 2022</time>\n                <!--\n         --></footer>\n        </div>\n    </a>","link":"https://inesmartins.github.io/when-not-to-use-jetpack-datastore/index.html","retrieved":1663200000000},{"title":"HTB Write-up | Paper","contents":"<a class=\"gh-card-link\" href=\"htb-write-up-paper/index.html\">\n            <figure class=\"gh-card-image\">\n                <img srcset=\"content/images/size/w160/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.37.25.png 160w,\n                           content/images/size/w320/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.37.25.png 320w,\n                          content/images/size/w600/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.37.25.png 600w,\n                         content/images/size/w960/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.37.25.png 960w,\n                        content/images/size/w1200/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.37.25.png 1200w,\n                       content/images/size/w2000/format/webp/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.37.25.png5.png 2000w\" sizes=\"320px\" src=\"content/images/size/w600/2024/11/Screenshot-2024-11-13-at-13.37.25.png\" alt=\"HTB Write-up | Paper\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            </figure>\n        <div class=\"gh-card-wrapper\">\n            <h3 class=\"gh-card-title is-title\">HTB Write-up | Paper</h3>\n                <p class=\"gh-card-excerpt is-body\">Write-up for Paper, a retired HTB Linux machine.</p>\n            <footer class=\"gh-card-meta\">\n<!--\n             -->\n                    <span class=\"gh-card-author\">By Inês Martins</span>\n                    <time class=\"gh-card-date\" datetime=\"2022-07-16\">16 Jul 2022</time>\n                <!--\n         --></footer>\n        </div>\n    </a>","link":"https://inesmartins.github.io/htb-write-up-paper/index.html","retrieved":1657929600000},{"title":"Creating a very spammable endpoint with Oracle APEX Restful Services","contents":"<a class=\"gh-card-link\" href=\"creating-a-very-spammable-endpoint-with-apex-restful-services/index.html\">\n            <figure class=\"gh-card-image\">\n                <img srcset=\"content/images/size/w160/format/webp/2022/05/email-spam.jpeg 160w,\n                           content/images/size/w320/format/webp/2022/05/email-spam.jpeg 320w,\n                          content/images/size/w600/format/webp/2022/05/email-spam.jpeg 600w,\n                         content/images/size/w960/format/webp/2022/05/email-spam.jpeg 960w,\n                        content/images/size/w1200/format/webp/2022/05/email-spam.jpeg 1200w,\n                       content/images/size/w2000/format/webp/2022/05/email-spam.jpeg.jpeg 2000w\" sizes=\"320px\" src=\"content/images/size/w600/2022/05/email-spam.jpeg\" alt=\"Creating a very spammable endpoint with Oracle APEX Restful Services\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            </figure>\n        <div class=\"gh-card-wrapper\">\n            <h3 class=\"gh-card-title is-title\">Creating a very spammable endpoint with Oracle APEX Restful Services</h3>\n                    <p class=\"gh-card-excerpt is-body\">I'm helping an organisation that has a very simple (and very static) corporate website. They were interested in adding a contact form, and wanted the data to be sent to their APEX-managed database.\n\nBuilding an entire back-end service for this purpose seemed like too much work, &nbsp;so I</p>\n            <footer class=\"gh-card-meta\">\n<!--\n             -->\n                    <span class=\"gh-card-author\">By Inês Martins</span>\n                    <time class=\"gh-card-date\" datetime=\"2022-05-07\">07 May 2022</time>\n                <!--\n         --></footer>\n        </div>\n    </a>","link":"https://inesmartins.github.io/creating-a-very-spammable-endpoint-with-apex-restful-services/index.html","retrieved":1651881600000},{"title":"HTB Write-up | Previse","contents":"<a class=\"gh-card-link\" href=\"htb-write-up-previse/index.html\">\n            <figure class=\"gh-card-image\">\n                <img srcset=\"content/images/size/w160/format/webp/2022/01/Screenshot-2022-01-05-at-15.03.17.png 160w,\n                           content/images/size/w320/format/webp/2022/01/Screenshot-2022-01-05-at-15.03.17.png 320w,\n                          content/images/size/w600/format/webp/2022/01/Screenshot-2022-01-05-at-15.03.17.png 600w,\n                         content/images/size/w960/format/webp/2022/01/Screenshot-2022-01-05-at-15.03.17.png 960w,\n                        content/images/size/w1200/format/webp/2022/01/Screenshot-2022-01-05-at-15.03.17.png 1200w,\n                       content/images/size/w2000/format/webp/2022/01/Screenshot-2022-01-05-at-15.03.17.png7.png 2000w\" sizes=\"320px\" src=\"content/images/size/w600/2022/01/Screenshot-2022-01-05-at-15.03.17.png\" alt=\"HTB Write-up | Previse\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            </figure>\n        <div class=\"gh-card-wrapper\">\n            <h3 class=\"gh-card-title is-title\">HTB Write-up | Previse</h3>\n                    <p class=\"gh-card-excerpt is-body\">Retired machine can be found here.\n\n\nScanning\n\nAs always, we start by mapping the previse.htb hostname to the given IP:\n\n~ sudo nano /etc/hosts\n\n10.10.11.104  previse.htb\n\nThe nmap scan is pretty boring, it seems there's a web server running on port 80 and</p>\n            <footer class=\"gh-card-meta\">\n<!--\n             -->\n                    <span class=\"gh-card-author\">By Inês Martins</span>\n                    <time class=\"gh-card-date\" datetime=\"2022-01-21\">21 Jan 2022</time>\n                <!--\n         --></footer>\n        </div>\n    </a>","link":"https://inesmartins.github.io/htb-write-up-previse/index.html","retrieved":1642723200000}]}